        "id": "U3-D2",
        "statement": "I kept Accounts as a Set and added a second set instead of replacing both with Map\u003CAccountId, status\u003E. The Map would make an id that is both open and closed impossible to represent, but it would change the type of the public Accounts field that existing code and tests read. The invariant that the sets do not overlap is documented on the type and kept because only openAccount and closeAccount change either set.",
        "basis": "evidence",
